// the value operand is an ordinary call argument now, so a wrong type is reported the way every other
// argument mismatch is - against the one operator the container declares, and naming the **value**.
//
// which operand gets named is AST::can_instantiate's business: `V` is mentioned by the receiver and by the
// value, and argument 0's bindings are authoritative - so `V` binds from the type the author declared and
// the value is what has to fit. bound from the value instead, this blamed the receiver
map<string, int32> $m = map<string, int32>();

$m['a'] = 'not an int';
